  "scope": "Spatial coordinate covariance requires more than onsite affine metric kinematics. A specified lattice product vacuum has a nonvanishing commutator defect density. An explicit finite shear is not unitarily implementable in a fixed massless scalar Fock representation in two or more dimensions, applying also to the metric trace if that channel is assigned this independent Fock representation. A metric-carried Gaussian covariance repairs kinematic transport between representations. This is established representation theory with an explicit repository diagnostic; it does not rule out quantum gravity or derive its microscopic phase, constraints or TOE."
